From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:46:22 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 40/46] doc: the iCE40 GPIO load through /dev/gpiomem on a
 Raspberry Pi 1-4

The Lattice page says which backend runs where and why (/proc/device-tree/
compatible), the register offsets and their documents, that a pin in an
alternate function is refused, that the functions are saved and put back,
that the clock is padded under 20 MHz, and that a BCM283x host whose
/dev/gpiomem is absent or closed stops loud with no libgpiod fall-back. The
warning now states the 17 Oct 2026 measurement (libgpiod 0.440 MHz on a Pi 3
Model B+) and that the /dev/gpiomem path is not yet tried on hardware.

Also corrected: a stall does not stop the load by itself; only a stall that
pulls the rate of one 4 KiB chunk under 1 MHz does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JG8Wtod8kFmcquwN34pFCa
